-- **User↔entity cardinality:** `entity_memberships` is N:N by design (allows future multi-entity). In MVP, "one user per entity" rule is enforced in application; no global UK on `user_id`.
-- **Owner and circular FK:** `entities.owner_membership_id` points to the membership with `role = owner`. Since `entity_memberships.entity_id` references `entities`, the FK is circular — on bootstrap, create entity with `owner_membership_id` null, create owner membership, then fill the FK (or use deferrable constraint). Ownership transfer updates this FK and involved roles.
+- **User↔entity cardinality:** `entity_memberships` is N:N by design (allows future multi-entity). "One membership per user per entity" is enforced by the unique index `entity_memberships_entity_user_unique` on `(entity_id, user_id)`; there is no global UK on `user_id`.
+- **Owner without a circular FK:** there is no `owner_membership_id` on `entities`. The owner is the membership with `role = owner`. A stored generated column `entity_memberships.owner_seq` is `1` when `role = 'owner'` and `NULL` otherwise; the unique index `entity_memberships_one_owner` on `(entity_id, owner_seq)` lets each entity have at most one `1`, while `NULL`s never collide in a unique index (SQLite and MariaDB alike). Different entities each have their own owner. Read the owner with `Entity::owner()`. Ownership transfer is a role change on two memberships and belongs to the transfer action.
